It's getting dark very soon. In a few hours you can see only the nearest trees, lit by the fire, and all the rest behind them is hidden in pitch-darkness.
You all tired and scared, but it's difficult to get to sleep. The jungle outside is full of weird and dreadful sounds. In thickets unknown animals howl and scream in fear, you can often hear strange rustles. Some apelike creatures came down the trees and look at your fire with curiosity. You look at them.
Suddenly these creatures begin to scream loudly, being frightened. One by one they rush up on the trees with a lightning speed. For a moment, silence fall upon the jungle. Then, branches on the trees are being pushed apart and a large, hairy, coal-black beast steps out to the glade.
Its long messy hair hangs down, with its saber long fangs gleaming in the light of the fire. The beast stands still looking at your fire. The creature`s nostrils move, it obviously scents you.
The predator comes closer, and then stops, hesitating, as if some unseen barrier restrained it. A few tedious minutes pass, that seem an eternity. Finally, the monster roars with disappointment, turns around and goes back into the thicket.
Your heart is thumping madly. Then tiredness takes over and you start falling asleep. Your last thought is that you ought to sleep in turns, so as to keep fire.